On Tue, 25 Nov 2003 21:11:26 GMT
Rob Ellwood <rob.ellwood@shaw.ca> wrote:
> 	Divine de-engulfification is of limited value if you're
> immediately re-engulfified.  Perhaps make the monster afraid?
> This fits in well with your "roars in divine fear" message.

OK, here's an updated patch. This addresses two issues:

1) Purple worms are MS_SILENT so they probaly can't roar. Make the
engulfer 'writhe' if MS_SILENT, otherwise use its growl_sound. However,
I don't think there are any non-MS_SILENT engulfers in the game as of
right now.

2) Scare the engulfer for rnd(10) + 5 turns after regurgitating you to
avoid immediately being swallowed again.

Also note that the previous patch was munged by my MUA's linewrapping
procedures. Hence this time it's attached as pray_expel.diff.

RFC desired!

-- 
Joshua Kwan

